{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist","id":817020,"title":"Similarities between Beast and Geist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-26T11:34:35-08:00","id":817020,"title":"Similarities between Beast and Geist","content":"How is Beast: The Primordial different from Geist: The Sin-Eaters?<br /> Fundamentally, they seem very similar in their Lore. The PCs have a catalytic event (Death/Beast-inspired Nightmare), and are offered a chance to become more than what they are (The Bargain/Devouring). They've always had a connection to the unseen (Ephemera/Primordial Dream). Their 'reawakening' is accompanied by a connection to a powerful entity, connected to archetypes base in human mythology (Geist/Horror). These ephemeral entities push the Sin-Eater/Beast towards goals unique to their archetype, acting as a disparate entity who can at best be described as amoral.<br /> Anyone can become these, provided they are not already supernaturally tainted by a Major Template.<br /> <br /> The major difference that I see is the Hero pseudo-mechanic (which I may start to incorporate into my other WoD works alongside Chambers), and the fact that Beasts as a whole have more direction than a 'motley Krewe' of Sin-Eaters. Leaving aside that they have differences in ability, I hold that their powers are less evocative in a storytelling game than their themes; I see a marked similarity in these themes, and that is what I am addressing.<br /> <br /> One could say that the above are near-tropes available in all CWoD and CofD lines, though I would posit that these themes are more pronounced (and done so in more similar ways) than in other titles. Changeling and Werewolf are stories about identity, living with a foot in two worlds; they are reflections of each other in many ways, yet different enough that I've even seen people refuse to let them mix. Beast and Geist seem too close together, with a piece of a chronicle-seed floating around in my head that Horrors may just be sufficiently powerful Geists anchored not to one keystone and person, but to many Lairs and Children.<br /> I'm still very excited to use Beast, and reading it through has re-invigorated my interest in the American supernatural Gary Stu show, Grimm.<br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","user":"Necrophear","date":". 01-26-2016, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T16:17:20-08:00","id":817229,"title":"","content":"From what I can tell, both Geist and Beast delve into the human soul, but in two different areas; what happens to it once death comes, and what the effects of fear may do to it. It's even specifically stated (at least in the pre-kickstarter edition) that Beasts don't really have governance over death, and that making a kinship with a Sin Eater opens up those kinds of possibilities for them. Sin Eaters, while utilizing fear, are able to approach things from a variety of different angles, whereas Beasts are more inclined for the terror aspect.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Sin Eaters tend to have a lot more utility to their powers than Beasts do, at least by default. Ceremonies by and large are able to do things that Nightmares cannot do, generally beneficial things as well as negative, and though Beasts are able to empower other supernaturals they don't have the same capabilities. Manifestations, while maybe not as powerful as Atavisms, likewise have a lot of different utility to them that Sin Eaters can dial up or down depending on what they want to do. Atavisms, meanwhile, while having different levels of power they can utilize are much more situational in terms of benefits others.<br /> <br /> There's also the way that the Geist/Horror interacts with their host that differs. For all intents and purposes, a Beast's Horror is their soul - it shapes their intents and behavior when their satiety goes low, and barring trying to kill/starve it I can't think of a way to degrade relations with one's Horror. Geists, on the other hand, are a separate entity (somewhat), which relations must be kept up with in order to have a functioning relationship. Furthermore, Geists don't need sating to stay in tandem with them - sure, you can do things that'll piss them off, but they don't require as much constant maintenance as a Horror does, nor are they (generally) as dangerous to others if relations with them degrade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T17:45:32-08:00","id":817273,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be opposed to making a Beast whose Horror had some kind of connection to death or oblivion. Fear of ending or Nothingness are each primal archetypes in the collective psyche, and so it makes sense that the Primordial Dream would contain something that hungers for those fears; by proxy creating Beasts that inspire lessons based upon them.<br /> <br /> I agree that the utility of Sin-Eaters would be a tier or two above those of Beasts, partially by route of how Beast was designed. They are very much the &quot;lesser&quot; siblings and amalgams of each of their supernatural kin. I very much enjoy the 'cousin of the Strange' concept, and hope to play with that dynamic more.<br /> I disagree with your interpretation of the relationship between Beast and Horror (first and foremost that it seems rather plain in what I am reading that there is one Horror for multiple Beasts, and so is not replacing a Devoured soul with its entirety), but admit that with no mechanical expy (like unto Synergy and Discord with one's Geist) there is little to say that the Horror's whispers are much more than a superfluous social/mental pressure.<br /> <br /> It would lay on the Storyteller to decide whether a Horror could take offense to the actions of a single Beast they've connected to. I'll probably marry the concepts of required feeding (Satiation/Vitae) with a little bit more required digging into esoteric mystery to unlock the full potential of your connection to a Horror (by way of Sin-Eaters/Mage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","user":"Necrophear","date":". 01-26-2016, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T20:11:41-08:00","id":817360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necrophear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=817273#post817273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with your interpretation of the relationship between Beast and Horror (first and foremost that <b>it seems rather plain in what I am reading that there is one Horror for multiple Beasts</b>, and so is not replacing a Devoured soul with its entirety)</div> </div> </div> </div>You are completely wrong even setting aside that the nomenclature for a Beast's mythic self in the first drafts was &quot;Soul&quot; rather than &quot;Horror.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T20:14:59-08:00","id":817363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necrophear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist#post817020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone can become these, provided they are not already supernaturally tainted by a Major Template.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not entirely true. Sin-Eaters need to start off as someone with affinity for the dead. As in a necromantic-bloodline's ghoul, or a Medium, or something similar. Can't make the Bargain without some sort of power to interact with ghosts on some level.<br /> <br /> As for Beasts? There IS a genetic component of some kind there. Its kind of like Werewolf; you were born with the inclination, but you don't awaken your full potential until the First Change / Devouring. Random Joe on the street might have that component, but if he doesn't? No chance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T22:00:41-08:00","id":817403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necrophear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=817273#post817273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be opposed to making a Beast whose Horror had some kind of connection to death or oblivion. Fear of ending or Nothingness are each primal archetypes in the collective psyche, and so it makes sense that the Primordial Dream would contain something that hungers for those fears; by proxy creating Beasts that inspire lessons based upon them.<br /> <br /> I agree that the utility of Sin-Eaters would be a tier or two above those of Beasts, partially by route of how Beast was designed. They are very much the &quot;lesser&quot; siblings and amalgams of each of their supernatural kin. I very much enjoy the 'cousin of the Strange' concept, and hope to play with that dynamic more.<br /> I disagree with your interpretation of the relationship between Beast and Horror (first and foremost that it seems rather plain in what I am reading that there is one Horror for multiple Beasts, and so is not replacing a Devoured soul with its entirety), but admit that with no mechanical expy (like unto Synergy and Discord with one's Geist) there is little to say that the Horror's whispers are much more than a superfluous social/mental pressure.<br /> <br /> It would lay on the Storyteller to decide whether a Horror could take offense to the actions of a single Beast they've connected to. I'll probably marry the concepts of required feeding (Satiation/Vitae) with a little bit more required digging into esoteric mystery to unlock the full potential of your connection to a Horror (by way of Sin-Eaters/Mage).</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting the idea that there is more than one Beast per Horror? First and foremost while on the forum we'll generally talk about the Horror and the Beast like they're separate entities they are not really different. A few people have described the Horror as something like the id and as Satchel pointed out originally Horrors were called the Soul.<br /> <br /> Also the Horrors don't whisper hell they don't even really drive the Beasts actions. A Beast's Horror only cares about eating, so its more like an eternally growling stomach. The thing is the Horror does nothing to push for feeding beyond being there and maybe go out on its own if you've been starving for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T00:21:27-08:00","id":817451,"title":"","content":"While some of this might be subject to change with a 2e Geist book:<br /> <br /> I think the difference is most pronounced looking at a simple comparison. Synergy vs. Satiety.<br /> <br /> Synergy is about two separate beings working together. A high Synergy Sin-Eater represents a Bound and Geist closely aligned in actions. Dropping to being one of the Wretched means the two have become inseparable but completely disconnected as they battle over control of a single body with no cohesion between different states. Maintaining a relatively high Synergy is purely a good thing for the dual-entity to exist.<br /> <br /> Satiety is simply about keeping a dark hunger within a Beast fed. The connection between Beast and Horror doesn't change as it goes up and down. How well fed the Horror is simple dictates how a Beast interacts with their Hunger. There is no &quot;good&quot; level of Satiety. Do you want to be hungry, but sharp and full of raw power from the drive to hunt? Do you want to try to balance the Hunger to keep it easy to feed but the Horror sleepy and weak? Do you want to sate the Horror for a more subtle form of power in freedom and selective hunting, but risk putting the Horror to sleep and being weakened for it?<br /> <br /> For all the other differences, I think these traits are highly representative of the core reasons why these end up as very different games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:31:37-08:00","id":817742,"title":"","content":"Wait, what? OP, you appear to have a fundamental misunderstanding of the nature of Beasts. Or at least of the nature of the Horror. This is not some external entity with which you have a relationship. It isn't controlling you, and it doesn't talk to you; it's YOU. It's your own monstrous self. Your Id. If your Horror has a mythic identity, the person who remembers said mythic identity is YOU. If you want to, you can constantly be seeing through your Horror's eyes within your Lair. If you want to, you can also ignore your human body and just wander about in your Lair as your Horror by using instant actions to control its dream-body directly. It doesn't direct or control you except in the sense that your own feelings of hunger and thirst direct and control you. You can't make it unhappy except in the sense that you can make yourself miserable by not eating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:38:11-08:00","id":817907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=817363#post817363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sin-Eaters need to start off as someone with affinity for the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is no more present mechanically than a nascent Beast's connection to the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Beasts? There IS a genetic component of some kind there. Its kind of like Werewolf; you were born with the inclination, but you don't awaken your full potential until the First Change / Devouring. Random Joe on the street might have that component, but if he doesn't? No chance. </div> </div> </div>To quote the book: &quot;Beasts are a literal bloodline: False. While Beasts often refer to themselves as being descended from the Dark Mother and divide themselves into Families, the connection is supernatural, not genetic. Any human being can be a Beast \u2014 there is no particular ancestry or marker for it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again to quote the book, [pg 15] &quot;The Horror is a monster from the Primordial Dream, which rushes up to merge with the dreamer. It splits the dreamer\u2019s nightmare off from that of her Big Brother or Sister, and the dreamer \u2014 now a Beast \u2014 finds herself in her new Lair. The Horror is now part of her.&quot; [pg52] &quot;Sometimes, the Devouring just happens. The Horror ascends from the Primordial Dream, finds the dreamer, and consumes the thin veneer of humanity that was her soul.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't think it's fair to ignore the many parts of the book that say quite plainly that the Horror itself is a separate entity. Its form may be a result of the inhabited person's own expectations or personal dream logic, but that doesn't change that it is fundamentally an alien being.<br /> <br /> <br /> Separately, time and again in the book it mentions the Horror roaming separately from the Beast if it's kept at low Satiety. Nowhere can I find mechanics for it, but it's still present, and thus up to the ST how to handle that fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:48:52-08:00","id":817918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necrophear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=817907#post817907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Separately, time and again in the book it mentions the Horror roaming separately from the Beast if it's kept at low Satiety. Nowhere can I find mechanics for it, but it's still present, and thus up to the ST how to handle that fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's ample folkloric precedent for one's soul drifting through other worlds when they sleep, and that's exactly the timeframe that the Horror is described as acting autonomously. You're not finding mechanics for it because the mechanics are &quot;Beasts' unconscious minds wander, as unconscious minds are wont to do.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:02:34-08:00","id":817940,"title":"","content":"Folkloric precedent is not the same as printed material. If that's what the ST chooses to use while 'handling this fluff', that's all well and good, but it still seems an oversight not to at least have suggestions on how to run the experience. The Horror is *not* the Beast, despite their deep connection, at least according to the words laid out before us in the rulebook. It plays on similar territory as the removal of agency through social maneuvers/merits/disciplines/etc., or how the Disquiet is sometimes difficult to implement in a scenario where characters are unaware of a Promethean's presence. Though there is indeed a mechanical compulsion, the cause is external (just not in a completely literal sense of 'external', owing to the cosmological position of the Primordial Dream).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:11:59-08:00","id":817948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necrophear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=817940#post817940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Folkloric precedent is not the same as printed material.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Your Horror wanders around the Primordial Dream while you sleep&quot; is literally the printed material you're referencing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:16:45-08:00","id":817951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=817742#post817742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what? OP, you appear to have a fundamental misunderstanding of the nature of Beasts. Or at least of the nature of the Horror. This is not some external entity with which you have a relationship. It isn't controlling you, and it doesn't talk to you; it's YOU. It's your own monstrous self. Your Id. If your Horror has a mythic identity, the person who remembers said mythic identity is YOU. If you want to, you can constantly be seeing through your Horror's eyes within your Lair. If you want to, you can also ignore your human body and just wander about in your Lair as your Horror by using instant actions to control its dream-body directly. It doesn't direct or control you except in the sense that your own feelings of hunger and thirst direct and control you. You can't make it unhappy except in the sense that you can make yourself miserable by not eating.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually this doesn't really come out in the 2nd draft text or the (pre-)published version. At least the part where the thing devouring you was YOU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:26:18-08:00","id":817958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=817948#post817948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Your Horror wanders around the Primordial Dream while you sleep&quot; is literally the printed material you're referencing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the problem with this aspect of the game is, &quot;so what?&quot; There are no mechanics supporting <i>doing</i> anything with your Horror while it prowls around. In this way it more or less resembles a Geist (although Geist preserved some cWoD Wraith ideas of being bodyjacked by your id). IMO, the resemblance pretty much ends there. I'm not sure I grok the OPs point as one can make the same argument for all the game lines but, the explanations aren't on target either so...<br /> <br /> For me the labels provide enough of a difference. A revenant resembles a beast not at all. They come from different places, have different themes, and are supported by wholly different mechanics. Is this one core concept similar? Sure, but so is everything in a game where you roll dice. This is probably not a topic worth getting overly exercised about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:52:29-08:00","id":817979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=817951#post817951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually this doesn't really come out in the 2nd draft text or the (pre-)published version. At least the part where the thing devouring you was YOU.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even if you accept Devouring over Homecoming, the resulting entity left after the process of Devouring is complete and the human soul is nommed up by the hungry Horror is you. You aren't a human being spirit-ridden by a Horror. You're one of the Begotten. The Horror is now just as much you as the human fleshy bits are. If you were to separate your body from your Horror, your human consciousness would end. <i>You</i> would be the Horror, wandering in the Primordial Dream; you would probably lose most of your ability to behave like a human being, and you would probably no longer a playable character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:20:50-08:00","id":818034,"title":"","content":"There isn't a relationship with one's Soul in <b>Beast</b> anymore than you could have a relationship, or bargain with your own subconscious. There isn't potentially divided motivations between an external entity and your own precepts of morality.<br /> <br /> What do you think your Soul does when you let it starve it's hunger? It goes out and plays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:25:10-08:00","id":818036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necrophear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=817907#post817907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is no more present mechanically than a nascent Beast's connection to the Primordial Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its flat out in the beginning of the book. Its a requirement. A meaningless requirement, perhaps, since we don't start off as a medium, we just right into the Bargian. But its there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To quote the book: &quot;Beasts are a literal bloodline: False. While Beasts often refer to themselves as being descended from the Dark Mother and divide themselves into Families, the connection is supernatural, not genetic. Any human being can be a Beast \u2014 there is no particular ancestry or marker for it.&quot; </div> </div> </div> I didn't say anything about a bloodline. I said you had an inclination. There's a difference. <br /> <br /> Since you seem quite fond of quoting, here's one from the Introduction. <br /> <br /> &quot;You were normal, once. At least more than you are now. You got up and went about your daily routine like anyone else \u2014 work, school, family, friends \u2014 with the same petty complaints and ambitions as anyone else you knew, except that you never quite fit in. People might have called you a troublemaker, a tattletale, a great judge of character, or an empath. You might know the truth, though: you dream deep.<br /> <br /> Your dreams pull you down into horrific, dark places with unholy monsters. Maybe they swoop down upon you from above, leaving you feeling exposed and vulnerable when you wake. Perhaps you dream of drowning, of tentacles yanking you into blackened deeps, or maybe your nightmares see you wandering in a dark wood with only an occasional growl to tell you of the creature that seeks your heart\u2019s blood. Whatever the nature of your nightmares, when you wake, things make sense. You sweat, your heart pounds, but in fear you find wisdom. Many people draw strength and perspective from their dreams, but yours give you purpose.<br /> <br /> Then came the day when you came face to face with a monster.&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems pretty clear to me that there's some kind of connection to dreams that pre-Horror Children have. They stand out a bit from other humans. &quot;At least more than you are now.&quot; Implying that something was always different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think it's fair to ignore the many parts of the book that say quite plainly that the Horror itself is a separate entity. Its form may be a result of the inhabited person's own expectations or personal dream logic, but that doesn't change that it is fundamentally an alien being. </div> </div> </div> Arguably before the Merging, they were separate. After? Its blantly clear that they're now a single being. The Horror <i>ate and replaced your soul</i>. Your soul and body aren't separate things - they're interlinked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Separately, time and again in the book it mentions the Horror roaming separately from the Beast if it's kept at low Satiety. Nowhere can I find mechanics for it, but it's still present, and thus up to the ST how to handle that fluff. </div> </div> </div> It mentions, time and again, the Horror roaming separately <i>while the beast keeps their body in the physical world and isn't inside the Lair. </i>Which doesn't mean much. You can literally enter your own head space and meet your shoulder angel and shoulder devil and have tea with them. That's the nature of the Astral/Physical world duality. The Astral isnt' a separate realm like the Hisil. Its an alternative way at looking at <i>this</i> world. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:51:58-08:00","id":818054,"title":"","content":"Actually it would be closer to the case of Kina of Swanmere from Exalted than arguing the Beast is a separate entity. For the uninitiated, in Exalted there are things called Hungry Ghosts will crop up when a person dies if the proper burial procedures aren't taken. In the case of Kina her Hungry Ghost goes out at night, as they do, and kills people, again like they do, with only one real difference from a normal Hungry Ghost. That difference being that Kina isn't dead, so her lower soul isn't leaving her corpse its detaching itself from her higher soul and leaving her body to feed. Now the reason I bring this up is simple that's what the Horror does when you've been starving too long and the thing is the Hungry Ghost is still Kina, just a part of her instead of the whole. So that whole thing mentioned that the Horror going out to eat when you've been starving too long proving that the Horror isn't part of the Beast is not a viable argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:04:27-08:00","id":818065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=817451#post817451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While some of this might be subject to change with a 2e Geist book:<br /> <br /> I think the difference is most pronounced looking at a simple comparison. Synergy vs. Satiety.<br /> <br /> Synergy is about two separate beings working together. A high Synergy Sin-Eater represents a Bound and Geist closely aligned in actions. Dropping to being one of the Wretched means the two have become inseparable but completely disconnected as they battle over control of a single body with no cohesion between different states. Maintaining a relatively high Synergy is purely a good thing for the dual-entity to exist.<br /> <br /> Satiety is simply about keeping a dark hunger within a Beast fed. The connection between Beast and Horror doesn't change as it goes up and down. How well fed the Horror is simple dictates how a Beast interacts with their Hunger. There is no &quot;good&quot; level of Satiety. Do you want to be hungry, but sharp and full of raw power from the drive to hunt? Do you want to try to balance the Hunger to keep it easy to feed but the Horror sleepy and weak? Do you want to sate the Horror for a more subtle form of power in freedom and selective hunting, but risk putting the Horror to sleep and being weakened for it?<br /> <br /> For all the other differences, I think these traits are highly representative of the core reasons why these end up as very different games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expanding upon that: your Geist, even if rather inhuman most of the time and eerily human sometimes, was indeed human long ago. Besides maintaining a high Synergy, exploring the past of your Geist is suggested as a plot hook in the Geist core. They could have been a warrior-saint, one of the darkest serial killers in history, or just someone who had a really bad day and coped as best as they could. The proclivity to be a part of death-tainted events and phenomena is a given, but Geister can come from all walks of life.<br /> <br /> Horrors, on the other hand, don't have the same versatility in backstory terms. They might have been an Incarnate that inspired a whole mythology and was served by other monsters who were nightmarish in their own right. With the exception of the Mimir's Wisdom Atavism, a Horror can't teach you anything new, because the Horror isn't someone else. A Geist, however, might have whole swathes of forgotten and rich history stored in its immaterial mind. There's a 3 dot Ceremony from page 161 of the G:tS core that allows you to extract information from your Geist, who is explicitly referred to as a separate entity. <br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters have to worry about the hopes, fears and other human-like traits of their Geister (such as they are), but they can count on the Geist to help in a pinch if they work as a team.<br /> <br /> Beasts are hosts to entities with no such frivolities, but cannot expect their Horror to not invade the dreamscape when Ravenous.<br /> <br /> The question of who has the better deal is worth exploring in-character, I believe.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:13:53-08:00","id":818075,"title":"","content":"&quot;Okay, Patrick, tell us a bit more about the relationship between Beasts and these 'Horror' things...&quot;<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KQLfgaUoQCw\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KQLfgaUoQCw</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:22:58-08:00","id":818405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=817979#post817979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you accept Devouring over Homecoming, the resulting entity left after the process of Devouring is complete and the human soul is nommed up by the hungry Horror is you. You aren't a human being spirit-ridden by a Horror. You're one of the Begotten. The Horror is now just as much you as the human fleshy bits are. If you were to separate your body from your Horror, your human consciousness would end. <i>You</i> would be the Horror, wandering in the Primordial Dream; you would probably lose most of your ability to behave like a human being, and you would probably no longer a playable character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well sort of. I agree it's never the case that your Horror takes you out for a ride around the town. However, your Horror is pretty much stuck in the Primordial Dream and you merging with it is pretty much you taking it out for a ride in its spirit skin. So the effect is rather 180 to the Geist approach where two entities share a body. Instead you're split across two bodies. The split is drastic that there's an entire section of a chapter devoted to what happens if you die, if your Horror dies, or if the two of you truly merge. Now you can can say that the Horror is YOU and on some metaphysical level I suppose that's true but the game's mechanics don't actually back it up very well.<br /> <br /> The intention that you are one being split across two bodies is pretty clear but you can only really play the human body and the Horror pretty much autopilots through life (possibly because its essential nature is as alien to us as angels, ghosts, spirits, and other ephemera) except for those few times you enter your/its lair and pseudo-merge with it. Your human body <b><i><u>is</u></i></b> separate from your Horror and resolving that issue is one of the features of the game. But we've rather sharply digressed from the OP's notion that Beast and Geist are similar games with similar themes, which I believe has been shown not to be the case in so far as any of the gamelines are similar/dissimilar to one another.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:00:48-08:00","id":818539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=818036#post818036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its flat out in the beginning of the book. Its a requirement. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's right in the beginning of the other book that the Beast-to-be has a connection to the Primordial Dream. I'm not sure if you're trying to disprove or prove this parallel, but the latter is what you've done with me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't say anything about a bloodline. I said you had an inclination. ... </div> </div> </div>What you said was that there is a genetic component, which the book flatly refutes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Arguably before the Merging, they were separate. After? Its blantly clear that they're now a single being. The Horror <i>ate and replaced your soul</i>. Your soul and body aren't separate things - they're interlinked. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't disagree with this, except to say that the book says that only a piece of the Horror is merging with the new Beast. That's the part we tinker with, creating the more personalized Horror; a reflection of the fears in an individual soul. The entity that spawned the Beast's Horror (the true child of the Dark Mother) remains separate.<br /> Jacob says it well, in that the game spends quite a lot of page-space devoted to the simple fact that the Horror is a separate entity connected to what was once a relatively normal human; an outside influence creating their Hunger and providing the perks of Beastdom. It is not shaped mechanically how it does this, which is IMO the fundamental disconnect between our interpretations of the text. The keyword being 'interpretation' of course, since this very important aspect of the nature of the Beast is left hazy; another parallel to a Geist, in fact.<br /> <br /> This discussion has shown me several new ways that the two games are similar, through causing me to reread the material a few times and the points brought up in discourse. I've also cemented several ways that the two games differ, and I thank the board for the new clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","user":"Necrophear","date":". 01-28-2016, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T05:12:15-08:00","id":820276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necrophear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=818539#post818539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't disagree with this, except to say that the book says that only a piece of the Horror is merging with the new Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not. It says that the Horror is now a part of the Beast, which does not mean that only a piece of the Horror is merging with the Beast.<br /> <br /> I know you don't want to believe it, but you're fundamentally misunderstanding the game if you think of Horrors as some separate entity that can bind with multiple Beasts, or that exists in any meaningful sense before the Beast himself did.<br /> <br /> GTS explicitly mentions that some Geists bind with multiple people, exist separately, etc. None of that is ever mentioned in Beast because it's not true. It's never explicitly stated that it isn't true because, again, the original text used the word Soul instead of Horror - and it would redundant to explicitly state that your Soul never bonded with other people before you were born. The Beast is the Horror. They are the same entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T08:42:52-08:00","id":821015,"title":"","content":"The thing to remember is that Horrors are <i>astral </i>entities. The Primordial Dream is the bit right at the base of the Temenos, just before it shifts into the Anima Mundi. This is important because the Temenos <i>isn't </i>a seperate realm of existence. It's the <i>collective soul of humanity.</i> So when a horror devours your soul what's really happening is that your soul is effectively devouring itself, and being replaced by something created from the soul-fabric of the entire world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:17:36-08:00","id":823768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=820276#post820276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...or that exists in any meaningful sense before the Beast himself did... It's never explicitly stated that it isn't true because, again, the original text used the word Soul instead of Horror - and it would redundant to explicitly state that your Soul never bonded with other people before you were born. The Beast is the Horror. They are the same entity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To reiterate quoted sections: [pg 15] &quot;The Horror is a monster from the Primordial Dream, which rushes up to merge with the dreamer. It splits the dreamer\u2019s nightmare off from that of her Big Brother or Sister, and the dreamer \u2014 now a Beast \u2014 finds herself in her new Lair. The Horror is now part of her.&quot; [pg52] &quot;Sometimes, the Devouring just happens. The Horror ascends from the Primordial Dream, finds the dreamer, and consumes the thin veneer of humanity that was her soul.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't disagree that the Horror undergoes a personalized metamorphosis upon Devouring an individual's soul, creating the actual Beast and the part of the Horror that can be called a version of its original soul. That does exist as what is accurately described as a single entity. None of that changes whether the Horror existed before that individual was born; it certainly exists before their Devouring, which can happen late in life. The Horror as a whole exists before the Beast, and will continue to exist after the Beast and their connection dies, because it is a thing born/created/called by that 'collective soul of humanity' Elfive mentions; not the individual facet that that Beast experiences, mind you, but the entity which first had a bit broken off for that merging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:24:08-08:00","id":823774,"title":"","content":"IIRC whether or not horrors &quot;reincarnate&quot; as such between beasts is a matter of some debate among them. The horror that exists before the merging may simply be a facet of the Dark Mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:38:13-08:00","id":823789,"title":"","content":"The book supports Horrors existing as separate entities, Horrors being passed down between Siblings, all Horrors being faces of the Dark Mother, and allows for none of those to be true.<br /> I'm not a particular fan of the final option unless I'm comfortable enough with the system for intensive homebrew, so my preference is that the preceding three each be as true as possible.<br /> <br /> This preference leads me to the Dark Mother having created the equivalent of avatars, her true children being these aptly named Horrors. When a Beast has their soul Devoured, the Sibling serves as a conduit (or the Horror itself acts) for a fragment of the Horror's power to ascend from the Primordial Dream to subsume the soul, taking on characteristics which we see mechanically as the individual Horror which informs our character creation. Since this is fully supported by the flavour of the book unlike the Horror being nothing more than a perverted soul, and not refuted by the mechanics, this is what I'll go with.<br /> <br /> This thread has been immeasurably helpful. Thanks go out to each of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:45:32-08:00","id":823801,"title":"","content":"Like I said, it's astral. The soul is both devoured by <i>and</i> becomes the Horror, which is <i>also </i>simultaneously a new entity and an ancient facet of the soul of humanity. And the soul was also really the horror the whole time, but not exactly.<br /> <br /> Dream shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T16:05:19-08:00","id":823822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=823801#post823801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... it's astral... Dream shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suspiciously similar to 'a wizard did it', one of my least favourite phrases in gaming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It tends to be a result of writing oneself into a corner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T16:12:13-08:00","id":823833,"title":"","content":"Not at all. The way to think about the astral is like a big tree. Your individual soul is one branch, but as you go back toward the base it joins a bunch of other branches to form one big branch. That's the temenos. Your individual soul is a part of it, but at the same time it's <i>all</i> you soul. So the horror comes from the collective, which is also you. But is also everyone else as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T16:22:52-08:00","id":823847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necrophear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=823822#post823822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Suspiciously similar to 'a wizard did it', one of my least favourite phrases in gaming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It tends to be a result of writing oneself into a corner.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to avoid any of the Mage threads then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T16:35:44-08:00","id":823858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=823833#post823833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all. The way to think about the astral is like a big tree. Your individual soul is one branch, but as you go back toward the base it joins a bunch of other branches to form one big branch. That's the temenos. Your individual soul is a part of it, but at the same time it's <i>all</i> you soul. So the horror comes from the collective, which is also you. But is also everyone else as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good concurrent interpretation, and one I may use at some later point for a different chronicle.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/817020-similarities-between-beast-and-geist?p=823847#post823847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to avoid any of the Mage threads then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I do, and will. Magery, much like many anime, makes itself much less substantial by trying to quantify too much of the wrong stuff while leaving everything else open to interpretation; made much worse by a sect of fans who misuse psychology and physics. I'm sure it's fun for them. I prefer the unknowable certainty of Cthulhu magicks, rather than the enumerated guessworks of Mage. It makes for some contention at my gaming table sometimes, with some of us preferring to know how a ritual was done over acceptance that it had occurred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}